   "note": "Mesh surgery on the shipped Meshy sculpt. The DEF's riveted flywheel (rim ellipse ~9x18 px at (60,98), the -X face turned toward the viewer) is the sculpt's row of three riveted discs on the -X side; the DEF's small edge-on wheel at the right is the sculpt's pair of spiked wheels on the +X side. All five spin about -X at the DEF rate: luminance rivet tracking in the normalised ellipse gives 2 rivet pitches of ~33 deg per 10-frame cycle, counter-clockwise on screen (tools audit, docs/homm3_map_object_animation_audit.md), i.e. 6.6 deg per DEF frame. The DEF moves the rivets in bursts (two held frames per 5); the mesh spins at the mean rate. The spiked wheels' direction cannot be read from an edge-on sprite and is assumed to match. The steam from the stacks stays a vanilla_style_effect. The spiked wheels spin about their gold hub caps (hubModel), not their spiky outline's centre.",
